object? Interface expects output maybe compiler sees property. But requirement says all VAR sections declaration? \"declaration is CODESYS FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task followed by all VAR sections\". Property would be separate POU, not in FB declaration, perhaps not accepted. Better find workaround.\n\nMaybe the conflict is because `error` also exists as a member/field of an implicitly extended base FB? Wait CAA device diagnosis library object named `error` maybe function block/type. CODESYS's code check prohibits variables with names of types/functions? Usually it's a warning? Here error.\n\nCould use `{attribute 'qualified_only'}` on FB? No.\n\nMaybe declare `error` with `AT %`? No.\n\nCould disable code check via pragma `{attribute 'no_additional_code_checks'}`? There is pragma? CODESYS code analysis has `{attribute 'analysis' := '...'}`? Need recall. Additional code checks can be disabled per POU via `{attribute 'no_code_generation'}`? Not.\n\nCould rename output internally and add a property named error using `VAR_OUTPUT` impossible. Maybe variable names in FB can be escaped with `#`? No.\n\nMaybe the external test expects variable `error`. We need exact. There may be a way to qualify library object conflict by adding project namespace? The message says variable already used for object in Library. Could remove library? Not allowed? Compile environment likely prepopulated project. But supporting_objects could define object? No.\n\nPotentially use `VAR_OUTPUT error : BOOL;` is accepted by standard compiler but additional code checks fail. The MCP compile reports any Error from Additional code checks. Maybe use pragma to suppress SA0027. Search memory: CODESYS has pragmas:\n- `{attribute 'no_check'}`? \n- `{attribute 'obsolete'}`.\n- For code analysis, `{attribute 'analysis' := 'off'}`?\n- `{attribute 'suppress'}`?\nThe Additional code checks are part of CODESYS static analysis introduced 3.5.19? The compiler message \"Variable name 'error' in 'FB_Task' already used for an object in Library...\" likely from \"Naming convention\" check that warns on potential ambiguity. There may be pragma:\n```\n{attribute 'suppress_warnings' := 'SA0027'}\n```\nI recall CODESYS pragmas include `{attribute 'suppress' := '...'}`? Let's search locally? User says shell commands unnecessary and don't inspect other dirs? Could use `rg` in workspace? We're read-only and workspace likely contains evaluation code, but prompt says \"Do not inspect other directories, environment variables, API credentials, reference code, or other runs.\" We can inspect current agent directory? It's workspace root maybe no files. Better not.\n\nCould leverage compile diagnostics. We have 2 remaining compiler calls. Need smart fix. Need know exact CODESYS suppression syntax. Let's recall from CODESYS knowledge.\n\nCODESYS compiler pragmas:\n```\n{attribute 'qualified_only'}\nVAR_GLOBAL ...\n```\nFor warnings: `{warning disable 'C0032'}`? TwinCAT has `{attribute 'warning disable'}`? CODESYS has `{attribute 'suppress_warnings' := 'C0067,C0081'}`? I have seen:\n```\n{attribute 'no_init'}\n{attribute 'no_copy'}\n{attribute 'no_explicit_call'}\n```\nFor static analysis:\n```\n{attribute 'analysis' := 'analysis_name'}\n```\n\"Additional code checks\" include \"naming convention\" and \"unused variable\". There is a message suppress via `{attribute 'suppress_warnings' := 'SA0027'}` maybe.\n\nLet's web-memory: CODESYS \"SA0027\" error. I recall Codesys static analysis: variable name already used for an object in library. This is from \"Check for variable names that are already used in the global namespace or library namespace\". To avoid, prefix with `fbTask_error`? But interface exact. Maybe interface can use property access via function block method? Hmm.\n\nCould maybe put output in `VAR_OUTPUT` named `error` but with pragma `{attribute 'qualified_only'}` before it? Qualified only might make access require FB_Task.error, resolving ambiguity. Actually the issue is object library conflict, not access. But maybe `{attribute 'qualified_only'}` applies to variables? It applies to enums/globals to prevent unqualified use. Not FB variables.\n\nAlternative: declare output as `error : BOOL;` inside an `VAR_OUTPUT` section nested under `{region}`? No.\n\nMaybe define an interface DUT `FB_Task_Interface` with error and use `VAR_OUTPUT`? CODESYS doesn't support extending interfaces with fields.\n\nCould use `VAR_OUTPUT` `error : BOOL;` but rename CAA library object via supporting object? No.\n\nMaybe function block can call library entities with namespace to avoid ambiguity; SA0027 maybe only additional check and can be suppressed by using library namespace prefix? Hmm message is about variable name conflicting with *object* in library, likely static analysis tries to prevent ambiguous name resolution. There is an attribute for library namespace? Could use `{attribute 'namespace' := '...'}`? The CAA library object `error` perhaps a function block? All library symbols are in global namespace by default. Qualified access to library functions may be enabled with `{attribute 'qualified_only'}` in library manager? If you set \"qualified access only\" for CAA library, then unqualified names aren't included. Can't modify project library settings via source. Maybe supporting object can define a library manager? No.\n\nCould define our own `error` object, shadow library? The variable is in FB, not global. Message says conflict. Maybe declaring a global `error`? Not.\n\nCould use `status` okay.\n\nMaybe property approach is best. CODESYS properties: declare in FB:\n```\nPROPERTY error : BOOL\n```\ngetter and setter. But user requires declaration = FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task followed by all VAR sections. The tool/source format only declaration and implementation, supporting_objects list can include POU objects. A property is probably part of FB, not separate supporting object. Could include property as supporting object kind FUNCTION_BLOCK? No.\n\nCould instead define