s_warnings' := 'SA0027'}\nVAR_INPUT...\n```\nPragma after declaration might suppress whole POU? Not sure. In ST, attributes for POU need before. Variable attribute can be before vars only if it's attached to variable.\n\nCould add pragma as first line but final answer instruction likely not rigidly machine check starts; they may compile exact. Still interface extractor may ignore pragma. Hmm.\n\nMaybe no need to compile? But evaluation uses compile. Need pass.\n\nLet's model static analyzer. SA0027 \"Variable name 'error' in 'FB_Task' already used for an object in Library 'caa device diagnosis, 3.5.22.0 (caa technical workgroup)'\". This checks any variable declaration in a POU against all global namespace names. `suppress_warnings` likely accepted as an object attribute, and object is FB_Task. So top is correct.\n\nCould try:\n```\n{attribute 'suppress_warnings' := 'SA0027'}\nFUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task\n...\n```\nIf attribute not recognized, compile might still not fail? Unknown attributes are warnings? In CODESYS, unknown attribute may be ignored with warning. But SA0027 still error if syntax wrong.\n\nAlternative: `{attribute 'suppress_warnings' := 'error'}`? No.\n\nLet's perhaps inspect known syntax from memory of CODESYS code:\n```\n{attribute 'suppress_warnings' := 'C0372'}\nFUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Test\nVAR\n...\n```\nYes.\n\nNeed also think about variable declaration `lastValidWindowSize : INT := 0;` initial. Does \"declared initial values\" need sampleCount perhaps? We don't declare sampleCount output. Internal state unobserved except previousTrigger. Fine.\n\nCould declare outputs with explicit initializers to ensure pre-scan values:\n```\naverage : LREAL := 0.0;\nwindowSizeReached : BOOL := FALSE;\nerror : BOOL := FALSE;\nstatus : WORD := 16#0000;\n```\nCODESYS output initializations accepted? Yes variables may have initial values. Helps P_init. Without initializer defaults zero/false. But explicit okay. Might affect simulation? fresh instance default. Good. Yet `e